From a589619033b902920550ab526d1c8371a11500de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Cipoletti <adam@amcreativecoach.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 01:04:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 55/55] Cheaper canvas drawing, Object.assign, replaceChildren,
 sticky, :focus-visible
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Canvas, from a profile of Speedometer's Charts-chartjs (5,366 points, each a
filled and stroked circle):

  - HTMLCanvasElement::didDraw asked the renderer for contentBoxRect() once
    per drawing operation, and resolving the CSS padding and border was most
    of its cost. It only changes when the canvas is laid out, so it is kept
    until then.
  - Path caches its fast bounding rectangle. GraphicsContext computed it
    twice per drawn path with CGPathGetBoundingBox and the canvas computed it
    again for the dirty rectangle; every mutator goes through
    ensurePlatformPath(), so one flag there covers them all.
  - Path::clear() leaves the path empty instead of allocating a fresh
    CGMutablePathRef that beginPath() often never draws into.

Object.assign copies a plain object's properties straight out of its
structure, in order, when nothing about the source can observe the read: no
getters, no custom or non-enumerable properties, no indexed properties and no
override of property lookup. Values are read before any of them is assigned,
since assigning can run script that changes the source. Chart.js constructs
every point with Object.assign.

ParentNode.replaceChildren() is implemented natively. The polyfill emptied
the node one child at a time, which is a mutation record, a children-changed
notification and a style invalidation each; this replaces the children in one
or two batches. Note 604's replaceAllChildren() only accepts a single node —
several nodes arrive as a DocumentFragment, which it would have inserted into
the tree as a child (an assertion catches this in a debug build only).

position: sticky is accepted and serialized unprefixed; the layout support was
already there under -webkit-sticky, so this is a keyword. :focus-visible is
accepted as :focus, which stops a whole selector being dropped for containing
it, and stops querySelector(":focus-visible") throwing SyntaxError — that was
killing scripts outright on github.com, bbc.com and outlook.live.com.

JavaScriptCore turns off concurrent collection, concurrent barriers and
concurrent compilation on PowerPC: these Macs have one processor, so the
second thread only competes with the mutator for it.
